, missing the final by only 0.43 points. In 1995 she won the World Championships and the overall World Cup title. She then sustained a serious back injury and was out of competition for over a year. But in the 1997-98 season she returned to win four of the six World Cup events prior to the Nagano Olympics and entered the Games as the favorite. The 1997 World Champion was Australian " [:a {:href "/athletes/81764"} "Kirstie Marshall"] ", but like Stone in 1994, she failed to get thru qualifying. In the final, Stone took a big lead on the first jump with a perfectly executed back full-double full. In the second round she placed second to China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/99814"} "Xu Nannan"] " but was far enough ahead that she won the gold medal easily. Xu had been fourth after round one, but moved up to the silver medal with her back full-double full. The competition was held in difficult weather, with strong, gusty winds. The bronze medal went to " [:a {:href "/athletes/80724"} "Colette Brand"] " (SUI), who had won the 1992 Olympic demonstration event. In 1994, she had also been among the favorites, but failed to qualify for the final."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/82470"} "Nikki Stone"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "174.00 (4)"] [:td {} "193.00 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/99814"} "Xu Nannan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympe